WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.762 --> 00:00:03.562
- [Narrator] Located in a waterfront park

00:00:03.562 --> 00:00:07.757
known as the Gardens by the
Bay is Supertree Grove.

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:10.377
This mechanical forest
is a utopia for nature

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.256
in a very urban location.

00:00:12.256 --> 00:00:16.423
(bouncy, lively electronic music)

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.863
Supertree Grove was
commissioned by the Singapore

00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:23.191
government with the intention of raising

00:00:23.191 --> 00:00:25.309
the quality of life for its residents

00:00:25.309 --> 00:00:28.976
by enhancing greenery
and flora in the City.

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:35.776
This manmade mechanical forest
consists of 18 Supertrees.

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:42.308
The trees range between
80 to 160 feet high

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.368
and are connected by a
walkway, which allows visitors

00:00:45.368 --> 00:00:47.923
to cross between them and view the City

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:49.423
from the treetops.

00:00:51.042 --> 00:00:53.823
With their thick trunks
and network of thin, neuron-like

00:00:53.823 --> 00:00:57.990
branches, each tree
acts as a vertical garden.

00:01:01.191 --> 00:01:05.179
Over 160,000 varieties of orchids, ferns,
and other climbing plants

00:01:05.179 --> 00:01:07.970
have been planted in the trees.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.271
The trees also generate solar power.

00:01:10.271 --> 00:01:13.890
11 of the trees are fitted
with solar photovoltaic systems

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.231
that convert sunlight into energy.

00:01:16.231 --> 00:01:18.161
This provides lighting
that allows the trees

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:21.151
to come alive at night,
making this an all day,

00:01:21.151 --> 00:01:23.734
all season horticultural heaven.

00:01:36.605 --> 00:01:38.772
(chiming)

